---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';import {planets,planetFacts,num} from '../../lib/planets.mjs';
---
<Layout title="The 8 Planets: Facts, Sizes & Comparisons" description="Facts for all eight planets in our solar system — size, gravity, mass, distance from the Sun and year length, from Mercury to Neptune, with NASA images and data." section="Planets" crumbs={[['Planets']]}><div class="wrap"><div class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Our cosmic neighborhood</span><h1>Eight worlds.<br/>Endless perspective.</h1><p>From sun-scorched rock to distant ice giants. Explore the eight planets of the solar system, then compare the numbers that make each world its own: size, gravity, mass, distance and the length of a year.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/planets/compare/">Compare planet sizes ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/labs/gravity-calculator/">Find your weight on another world</a></div></div><div class="planet-grid">{planets.map((p,i)=><a class="planet-card" href={`/planets/${p.id}/`}><img src={`/images/${p.id}.webp`} alt={`${p.name}, NASA mission imagery`} width="1024" height={p.id === 'saturn' ? 341 : 576} loading="lazy"/><div><span class="eyebrow">0{i+1} / {p.kind}</span><h2>{p.name} ↗</h2><p>{p.tag}</p></div></a>)}</div><section class="section"><h2>Put the planets in perspective</h2><p>Rounded reference values. Diameters are equatorial; orbital periods are Earth days. <a class="text-link" href="/planets/compare/">Sort every value on the comparison page ↗</a></p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Planet</th><th scope="col">Diameter (km)</th><th scope="col">Size vs Earth</th><th scope="col">Gravity (m/s²)</th><th scope="col">Orbit (days)</th><th scope="col">Distance (AU)</th><th scope="col">Mean temperature (°C)</th></tr></thead><tbody>{planets.map(p=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={`/planets/${p.id}/`}>{p.name}</a></th><td>{p.diameter.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td><td>{num(planetFacts(p).widthRatio,2)}×</td><td>{p.gravity.toFixed(1)}</td><td>{p.period.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td><td>{(p.distance/149.5978707).toFixed(2)}</td><td>{p.temp}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="worked">Reference: <a class="text-link" href="https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/factsheet/">NASA Planetary Fact Sheet</a>. Giant-planet temperatures and gravity refer to atmospheric levels, not a solid surface.</p></section></div></Layout>
